            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="EGE01" sex="1">
                    <persName><roleName/>Lord
    <forename>Francis</forename><surname>Egerton</surname><addName/>Leveson-Gower
  </persName>
                    <birth when="1800-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1857-02-18"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin wrote  to Lord Francis Egerton
      with respect to <persName key="PIC03">Janet Picken</persName> on 31 March 1835.  It is possible that early 
    references to Levison might be mispellings of 
    Egerton (i.e. Leveson) before he assumed the title, but there 
    is nothing to link Leveson with a lecture in January 
    1832 so we have discounted this possibility.</p>
                        <p> There are a range of earlier entries to Egerton in the Diary but these seem to be
    to  <persName key="EGE02">J Egerton</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
